So what to say... I don't know if I can recommend to others to play this game and here's why I say like that:
Pros:
+Good graphics;
+Almost lagless on over 30fps (even tho game tells me that it is lagging a lot -_-);
+Customization together with workshop's mods.
+I love main menu song - Regain Control but.... (<-I'll get to that pretty soon)
Well that's how far good stuff about game goes... Welp let me now get to nitty gritty negative stuff...
Cons:
-Rythm recognition in game is completely crap;
-Main menu song does not play on loop when you have to stay at main menu while tweaking settings and what not;
-It's really hard to find Desktop folder so I could find my music folder;
-Prolonged note quicktime events appear where in actual song there are little to no prolonged notes which would cause game to generate prolonged note quicktime events;
-Game doesnt recognise when I click a right button at right time (PS. this links together with 1st of Cons point);
So now let me go thru full explanation of some points... First of all what really bugged me while playing this game, is that game is quite dang crap at recognising proper rythm of song. Why I say this? Well, I go to choir and before for a long time I went to choir and there usually managing to sing out right note at right rythm is big thing, so I had good amount of excercises for my ears to recognise rythm of song without help from percussion in song and the songs which I played in game... I know those songs really well and I have heard them buttloads of times and I was surprised how whenever I clicked right rythm with button, game did not accepted that making my character fail. So please devs of this game... PLEASE improve rythm recognition system. Also I must note this down that, game is usually approx. 1sec off from real rythm of song. Now onto prolonged notes delio (hold on to yer chairs this review will be long)... Ergh, ok wtf? Why the f- game out of blue adds prolonged note quicktime event when playing songs which have little to no prolonged notes? Seriously, that is just plain wrong on many levels. I today played one song which doesnt even have vocals and has only like about 2 or 3 prolonged notes in whole song, yet game generated buttloads of prolonged notes quicktime events at completely wrong parts of song. On topic of finding songs in folders on your computer desktop... ergh I don't think it's even possible to do that in game and that really flippin sucks. Main menu song Regain Control doesn't loop on main menu when you have to stay for a lil longer on main menu screens while tweaking settings of game and that really makes me really sad since it is really good song and I quite like it.
Welp I would like to talk about not a lot of positive stuff about this game but I won't... I am legit dissappointed in this game. I don't think that I can recommend this to anyone and if devs of game wont fix obviously crappy rythm recognition system in that game, then I may aswell request for refund for this game. 9 Euros... Dude you would espect this game to be good but... sadly, it is not. If you want to be frustrated to no end while playing your favorite song, then go ahead and play this game. Otherwise, to me when song and game meet, the game has to give additional satisfaction when song plays, but here this doesn't happen at all. So big thumbs down from me to devs of this game.
Ps. "synced to the beats of your music of choice thanks to *very accurate beat detection*" <- thats ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥t, big lies because I myself recognised very accuratelly rythm of songs meanwhile game legitimatelly every time kept faceplanting into ground with crap recognition of rythm a.k.a beats in song aand ultimately game was approx. 1second off from right song rythm...

The concept of old-meets new is pretty interesting, and in some ways a new experience;
The art direction is amazing and manages to build the atmosphere very well. Worth spending some time admiring all the details!
Controls are simple to get, but can get very buggy, specially towards the end of the game, as you need faster imputs;
Story is very predictable, and felt cut short in the end;
Voice acting is weak, some actors either had zero drive, or they where simply terribly missplaced role-wise;
Game overall gets very buggy towards the end.
It´s a great addition if you just want to check out the amazing art.

I played game again, because I recall it's potential. TLDR; wait another year or maybe two.
Game has lots of problems. Many are solved over course of development, but there are still so many things are left before it's ready. I can't recommend it now. Wait year or two. I seen many dead early access games to recommend to buy this even with discount.
Good things:
- story mode is totally playable and enjoyable, quests are much easier to progress, storyline is intriguing,
;
- adventure mode feels really good, rising skills, hunting, fighting, making money, exploring;
- editor with templates and community made content is cool, it's easy to figure out things by looking at someone's creations;
- game doesn't crash at all (could be subjective as I had my PC upgraded);
Bad things:
- it needs polishing;
- it need bugfixes.
I am really up to play adventure mode, probably in multiplayer with friends, but I have too strong beta-tester-feelings when playing it. It's simply not ready yet.
