When I first started playing this game, I spent all my time in the single player campaign.  It offered countless hours of enjoyment (litterally countless since I played the non-Steam version for a long while).
Now, I've moved to the multiplayer/modding side of the game (I'm a developer for
) and it continues to be one of my most played games.  The modding system is not always easy to use but with enough time and effort, a lot can be accomplished - especially with some of the third party tools available through the TaleWorlds forum.

Pros: Good graphics for a 2001 game;
Fun and good platforming;
Taking care of chao is fun and time consuming;
While not too challenging, it still delivers some hard challenges, like the "Hard Mode" of each stage, which is a harder version of the original stages.
Cons: Glitches make the completion to 100%, frustrating;
Tails/ Eggman Stages are dull and shallow;
Rails are a bit inconsistent;
Homing attack has a chance of missing the target even if it's in range and at the right angle;
Biolizard is harder than the final boss.

GREAT GREAT GAME, HIGHLY RECOMMENDED!!!
This isn't just another zombie game;
this is a very engaging side scrolling game that has a few puzzle elements.
